cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Rhizome in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "Rhizome: a free, open-source explorer of the literature around any paper"
abstract: >-
  Rhizome builds an interactive graph of the papers most similar to a chosen paper,
  combining bibliographic coupling and co-citation computed from OpenAlex data, with
  prior and derivative works lists and BibTeX/RIS export for reference managers.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Tetteh
    given-names: Israel Tawiah
license: MIT
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-11-20"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Israel-Tetteh/rhizome"
url: "https://israel-tetteh.github.io/rhizome/"
keywords:
  - literature review
  - citation network
  - bibliographic coupling
  - co-citation
  - OpenAlex
  - research tools
references:
